/target
docs/target

.thndrs
.env
.zed

# Agent configuration is tracked. These negations keep the files in the
# repository when a global or editor ignore rule would otherwise drop them.
!CLAUDE.md
!AGENTS.md
!.claude/
!.claude/**
!.agents/
!.agents/**

# Local overrides stay out of the repository.
.claude/settings.local.json

# A worktree is a second checkout and its build tree, not work to commit. The
# negations above would otherwise track one a harness placed here, and the
# checkout would read dirty for as long as its agent runs. Agents create theirs
# outside the repository root; this catches the case nothing here controls.
.claude/worktrees/
